Elisp written for a recent Emacs reaches for things the older Emacsen
pkgsrc still carries do not have: hash tables over alists,
replace-regexp-in-string, propertize, subr-x's string functions,
setq-local, with-eval-after-load, prog-mode, syntax-ppss,
syntax-propertize, alist-get, seq-filter, delete-dups, and a regexp
translator for shy groups, intervals and [:alpha:] classes that Emacs
20's engine does not have.

Each is defined only when the running Emacs does not have it, so one
file serves every version and does nothing on an Emacs that has them
all.  The package is named for the Emacs it was built for, so a package
that needs any of this can require emacs-compat and keep one source.
